,"type":"Reroute","pos":[1953.9364013671875,-255.239990234375],"size":[82,26],"flags":{},"order":36,"mode":0,"inputs":[{"name":"","type":"*","link":132}],"outputs":[{"name":"MODEL","type":"MODEL","links":null}],"title":"MODEL","properties":{"showOutputText":true,"horizontal":false},"color":"#323","bgcolor":"#535"},{"id":86,"type":"Note","pos":[-693.9616088867188,-607.419677734375],"size":[476.9273681640625,150.90830993652344],"flags":{},"order":4,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"properties":{},"widgets_values":["Diffusion Models don't work directly with pixels. To save space, they use a smaller latent pixel space that reduces the size of the matricies involved.\nVAE's job is to turn RGB pixels into latent pixels (encode), and turn latent pixels into RGB pixels (decode).\n\nA fast low accuracy version of the VAE decode is used to show the progress in each step of the diffusion model in the KSampler\n\nFlux VAE:\nhttps://huggingface.co/black-forest-labs/FLUX.1-dev/blob/main/vae/diffusion_pytorch_model.safetensors"],"color":"#332922","bgcolor":"#593930"},{"id":66,"type":"Note","pos":[-1178.705078125,195.11244201660156],"size":[310.0617980957031,92.88003540039062],"flags":{},"order":5,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"properties":{"text":""},"widgets_values":["Generate an empty latent image.\n\nimg2img workflow will have image resize and VAE encode here\n\n"],"color":"#222","bgcolor":"#000"},{"id":30,"type":"CheckpointLoaderSimple","pos":[-1988.8668212890625,-425.695556640625],"size":[484.8478698730469,98],"flags":{},"order":6,"mode":0,"inputs":[{"localized_name":"ckpt_name","name":"ckpt_name","type":"COMBO","widget":{"name":"ckpt_name"},"link":null}],"outputs":[{"localized_name":"MODEL","name":"MODEL","type":"MODEL","slot_index":0,"links":[62]},{"localized_name":"CLIP","name":"CLIP","type":"CLIP","slot_index":1,"links":[]},{"localized_name":"VAE","name":"VAE","type":"VAE","slot_index":2,"links":[]}],"properties":{"cnr_id":"comfy-core","ver":"0.3.26","Node name for S&R":"CheckpointLoaderSimple"},"widgets_values":["flux1-dev-fp8-full.safetensors"],"color":"#323","bgcolor":"#535"},{"id":79,"type":"Note","pos":[-1993.44482421875,-614.6204833984375],"size":[493.861572265625,147.73858642578125],"flags":{},"order":7,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"properties":{},"widgets_values":["This is the diffusion models that turn latent pixels into latent pixels\nin incremental steps using a KSampler, a scheduler and a sampler\nI'm using an HiDream GGUF that is quantized down to save VRAM\n\nFlux FP8 model:\nhttps://huggingface.co/Aitrepreneur/FLX/blob/main/flux1-dev-fp8.safetensors\n\nFlux FP16 model:\nhttps://huggingface.co/black-forest-labs/FLUX.1-dev/blob/main/flux1-dev.safetensors"],"color":"#323","bgcolor":"#535"},{"id":83,"type":"Note","pos":[-1338.0528564453125,-747.0498046875],"size":[500.2712097167969,246.46270751953125],"flags":{},"order":8,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"properties":{},"widgets_values":["Diffusion Models have an high dimensional latent concept space that encodes\nthe latent pixel distribution of everything the model knows.\nCLIP task is to find the coordinates of the concept that you want to diffuse\ninside that latent concept space, so the model can diffuse that distribution\nin the latent pixel space.\n\nFlux has a CLIP and a Text Encoder.\n\nFlux CLIP L:\nhttps://huggingface.co/black-forest-labs/FLUX.1-dev/blob/main/text_encoder/model.safetensors\n\nFlux Text Encoder (FP8):\nhttps://huggingface.co/Aitrepreneur/FLX/blob/main/umt5_xxl_fp8_e4m3fn_scaled.safetensors\n\nFlux Text Encoder (FP16):\nhttps://huggingface.co/Aitrepreneur/FLX/blob/main/t5xxl_fp16.safetensors"],"color":"#432","bgcolor":"#653"},{"id":75,"type":"DualCLIPLoader","pos":[-1335.40283203125,-465.2155456542969],"size":[497.780517578125,130],"flags":{},"order":9,"mode":0,"inputs":[{"localized_name":"clip_name1","name":"clip_name1","type":"COMBO","widget":{"name":"clip_name1"},"link":null},{"localized_name":"clip_name2","name":"clip_name2","type"